### Testing against a live external repo

Some skills document a dependency on a real script or file living in a
separate, external repo (e.g. `cloud-sql-onboarding`'s `enable_cloud_sql.py`,
which lives in `caf-template-app-resources`, an Azure DevOps repo — not
this one). A case can clone that repo directly in its `scaffold:` — see
`skills/cloud-sql-onboarding/evals/enables-terraform-toggle-against-live-template/`.
This is a deliberate choice: **unpinned, always the live `template` branch**,
matching what the skill itself already assumes ("keep your local clone
pulled to latest") — the point is that a breaking change in the external
repo surfaces as an eval failure the next time this runs, not that the eval
stays stable forever. There's no separate drift-detection job; running
against live HEAD *is* the drift check.
